{
  "explanation": "The attacker utilized the automated tool 'sqlmap' from IP 193.32.162.40 to attempt SQL injection attacks against the '/catalog' and '/api/v2/session' endpoints. The payloads included UNION-based extraction attempts to enumerate database table names, time-based blind injections using SLEEP(), and authentication bypass techniques. The HTTP status codes (500, 504, 401) suggest that while some queries caused server errors or timeouts, the authentication attempts were appropriately blocked.",
  "mitre_tactic": "Initial Access",
  "recommended_actions": [
    "Implement parameterized queries or prepared statements across all database interactions to neutralize SQL injection vectors.",
    "Block the malicious source IP (193.32.162.40) at the Web Application Firewall (WAF) and perimeter firewall levels.",
    "Deploy a WAF rule set to automatically detect and drop requests containing automated SQL injection signatures such as 'sqlmap' user-agents and SQL syntax keywords."
  ]
}
